      "ref": "12.1.3",
      "name": "She Who Holds the Waters",
      "devanagari": "यस्यां समुद्र उत सिन्धुरापो यस्यामन्नं कृष्टयः संबभूवुः ।\nयस्यामिदं जिन्वति प्राणदेजत्सा नो भूमिः पूर्वपेये दधातु",
      "transliteration": "yasyāṁ samudra uta sindhurāpo yasyāmannaṁ kṛṣṭayaḥ saṁbabhūvuḥ\nyasyāmidaṁ jinvati prāṇadejatsā no bhūmiḥ pūrvapeye dadhātu",
      "translation": "On whom are the sea, the flowing rivers, the waters; on whom food and the tilled fields came to be; on whom breathes and stirs all that lives — may that Earth grant us the first draught."
