      "ref": "12.1.4",
      "name": "The Four Directions",
      "devanagari": "यस्याश्चतस्रः प्रदिशः पृथिव्या यस्यामन्नं कृष्टयः संबभूवुः ।\nया बिभर्ति बहुधा प्राणदेजत्सा नो भूमिर्गोष्वप्यन्ने दधातु",
      "transliteration": "yasyāścatasraḥ pradiśaḥ pṛthivyā yasyāmannaṁ kṛṣṭayaḥ saṁbabhūvuḥ\nyā bibharti bahudhā prāṇadejatsā no bhūmirgoṣvapyanne dadhātu",
      "translation": "Whose are the four directions; on whom food and the tilled fields came to be; who bears in a thousand ways all that breathes and moves — may that Earth set us among the cattle, and in abundance."
