      "devanagari": "महत्सधस्थं महती बभूविथ महान् वेग एजथुर्वेपथुष्टे ।\nमहांस्त्वेन्द्रो रक्षत्यप्रमादम् ।\nसा नो भूमे प्र रोचय हिरण्यस्येव संदृशि मा नो द्विक्षत कश्चन",
      "transliteration": "mahatsadhasthaṁ mahatī babhūvitha mahān vega ejathurvepathuṣṭe\nmahāṁstvendro rakṣatyapramādam\nsā no bhūme pra rocaya hiraṇyasyeva saṁdṛśi mā no dvikṣata kaścana",
      "translation": "Great you have become, a great abode; great is your trembling, your stirring, your quaking; and great Indra guards you without cease. Make us shine, O Earth, bright as the face of gold — and let no one hate us."
